  "authoringNote": "D1 reject contrast. A supporting-note title required nonblank text in v1 and uses ExactText in v2, so an empty or whitespace-only title makes the body fail the exact structured parse. A source body that fails to parse is never an assessment-wide rejection; it is R09 body_invalid (frozen D6 and R09). Both notes match their hashes, are available and are application/json, so body_invalid is the first applicable R09 condition for each: R09 is unreadable with two conditions, one per note, routed to the authorization coordinator (needs_information), and its parent set names both notes (C07). An unreadable version is bound by metadata only (both carry the case subject), so R02 passes without comparing or citing them; R02 cites the six facts of the encounter, order and receipt. No rule reads notes, so nothing else changes: R01, R03, R04, R05 and R07 pass with ordinary citations (eight, nine, six, four, one), R06 and R10 as always. State needs_information. The note text is not negative evidence.",
